   "source": [
    "# Application train: cleaning and preprocessing\n",
    "All processing code is written directly in this notebook, with explanations. No src package or pipeline scripts are needed.\n",
    "\n",
    "Sections 1-10 contain your inspection, initial cleaning, and split. Sections 11-21 create features, fill missing values, encode text, scale numeric values, verify results, and save the application-only handoff. Validation rows never fit preprocessing. No prediction model is trained and no other source CSV is processed here.\n",
    "\n",
    "Run All from the beginning after selecting your Python kernel. The original CSVs remain unchanged.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Load the original training data\n",
    "Import Path from pathlib and import pandas using the alias pd. Set data_folder to home-credit-default-risk, then read application_train.csv into df.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Your exercise:** display df.shape and the first five rows using head(). Expected size from our earlier inspection: 307,511 rows and 122 columns. If the file is not found, check the working directory before changing the path.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why:** this notebook needs its own imports and data loading so it can run independently. Read the original CSV without overwriting it.\n"
   ]
  },
