    "### Proposed missing-value decisions\n",
    "These are proposed strategies, not applied changes. We will finish the categorical and numerical investigations, split the labeled data, and fit replacement values using training rows only. Validation and future applications will use the same fitted replacements.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Feature or group | Proposed action | Reason | Status |\n",
    "|---|---|---|---|\n",
    "| Numeric features such as AMT_ANNUITY | Fill missing values with the training median | Provides a typical value less influenced by extremes than the mean | Pending; calculate after splitting |\n",
    "| Text features such as OCCUPATION_TYPE | Fill missing entries with an explicit Missing label before encoding | Preserves the fact that information was unavailable | Pending; implement in preprocessing |\n",
    "| DAYS_EMPLOYED | Flag the exact placeholder 365243, replace it with numeric missing, and later impute from training data | The placeholder is not a literal employment duration | Pending confirmed cleaning rule |\n",
    "| OWN_CAR_AGE | Retain FLAG_OWN_CAR, add an age-missing indicator, and later fill the numeric gap using the training median | Ownership distinguishes no car from a car with unrecorded age; the flag identifies imputed ages | Proposed; interpret section 5 group results before finalizing |\n",
    "| Features with large missing percentages | Review meaning and training-set missingness before deciding whether to retain or exclude | High missingness alone does not establish that a feature is useless | Pending training-set review |\n",
    "| Features entirely missing in training | Explicitly decide whether to exclude or retain with a defined fallback | A median cannot be estimated when no training values are recorded | Pending training-set review |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Example:** recorded training annuities of 10,000, 20,000, and 90,000 have median 20,000. That value would fill missing annuities in both training and validation; validation does not get a separately calculated median.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Next:** investigate categorical values in section 6. Do not fill values yet or replace every missing entry with zero. Update the main decision log when a rule is finalized and applied.\n"
   ]
  },
