   "source": [
    "## 15. Define numeric filling and scaling\n",
    "\n",
    "This uses standard scikit-learn objects, with all code visible here. The imputer will learn training medians in section 18. StandardScaler then adjusts numeric magnitudes for a Logistic Regression baseline. There is no fitted prediction model in this notebook.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 24,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Pipeline(steps=[('imputer', SimpleImputer(strategy='median')),\n",
      "                ('scaler', StandardScaler())])\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\n",
    "from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
    "\n",
    "numeric_pipeline = Pipeline([\n",
    "    (\"imputer\", SimpleImputer(strategy=\"median\")),\n",
    "    (\"scaler\", StandardScaler()),\n",
    "])\n",
    "print(numeric_pipeline)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 16. Define text filling and encoding\n",
    "\n",
    "Fill actual text gaps with __MISSING__, then learn one indicator column per training category. For example contract type becomes Cash loans and Revolving loans indicators. Unseen validation categories do not create new columns because handle_unknown is ignore.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 25,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Pipeline(steps=[('imputer',\n",
      "                 SimpleImputer(fill_value='__MISSING__', strategy='constant')),\n",
      "                ('encoder',\n",
      "                 OneHotEncoder(dtype=<class 'numpy.float32'>,\n",
      "                               handle_unknown='ignore'))])\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import OneHotEncoder\n",
    "\n",
    "categorical_pipeline = Pipeline([\n",
    "    (\"imputer\", SimpleImputer(strategy=\"constant\", fill_value=\"__MISSING__\")),\n",
    "    (\"encoder\", OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown=\"ignore\", sparse_output=True, dtype=np.float32)),\n",
    "])\n",
    "print(categorical_pipeline)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 17. Combine the numeric and text branches\n",
    "\n",
    "ColumnTransformer sends each column to its matching branch and joins the results. It is a standard scikit-learn object, not another project file you need to maintain. It has not been fitted yet. Numeric scaling is included for the first Logistic Regression baseline; a tree model can use a separate unscaled preparation later.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 26,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "ColumnTransformer(sparse_threshold=1.0,\n",
      "                  transformers=[('numeric',\n",
      "                                 Pipeline(steps=[('imputer',\n",
      "                                                  SimpleImputer(strategy='median')),\n",
      "                                                 ('scaler', StandardScaler())]),\n",
      "                                 ['CNT_CHILDREN', 'AMT_INCOME_TOTAL',\n",
      "                                  'AMT_CREDIT', 'AMT_ANNUITY',\n",
      "                                  'AMT_GOODS_PRICE',\n",
      "                                  'REGION_POPULATION_RELATIVE',\n",
      "                                  'DAYS_REGISTRATION', 'DAYS_ID_PUBLISH',\n",
      "                                  'OWN_CAR_AGE', 'FLAG_MOBIL', 'FLAG_EMP_PHONE',\n",
      "                                  'FLA...\n",
      "                                                  OneHotEncoder(dtype=<class 'numpy.float32'>,\n",
      "                                                                handle_unknown='ignore'))]),\n",
      "                                 ['NAME_CONTRACT_TYPE', 'CODE_GENDER',\n",
      "                                  'FLAG_OWN_CAR', 'FLAG_OWN_REALTY',\n",
      "                                  'NAME_TYPE_SUITE', 'NAME_INCOME_TYPE',\n",
      "                                  'NAME_EDUCATION_TYPE', 'NAME_FAMILY_STATUS',\n",
      "                                  'NAME_HOUSING_TYPE', 'OCCUPATION_TYPE',\n",
      "                                  'WEEKDAY_APPR_PROCESS_START',\n",
      "                                  'ORGANIZATION_TYPE', 'FONDKAPREMONT_MODE',\n",
      "                                  'HOUSETYPE_MODE', 'WALLSMATERIAL_MODE',\n",
      "                                  'EMERGENCYSTATE_MODE'])])\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer\n",
    "\n",
    "preprocessor = ColumnTransformer([\n",
    "    (\"numeric\", numeric_pipeline, numeric_columns),\n",
    "    (\"categorical\", categorical_pipeline, categorical_columns),\n",
    "], remainder=\"drop\", sparse_threshold=1.0)\n",
    "print(preprocessor)"
   ]
  },
